# Environment variable names (values live in deployment-env stores only — never in the repo)
# Supabase Edge Functions secrets + GitHub Actions secrets + Vercel project env hold the real values.
#
# 26 Oct 2026: the domain, Gemini's paid tier, a paid Supabase plan and Paddle approval are assumed
# done. See docs/GO-LIVE-REGISTER.md for what that changes and the only steps left (hosting, Paddle's
# catalog, domain email, migrations 0016-0026). Unset optional product prices are intentional: that
# product is then not sold, and the site says so instead of offering a checkout that cannot finish.

# ============================================================================
# USED BY THE APP AT RUNTIME (set these in Vercel → Project → Settings → Env)
# ============================================================================

# --- Hosts (single app; SINGLE HOST for the first deploy — marketing + auth + app on one origin) ---
# Set SITE_URL / MARKETING_HOST to the Vercel URL now and to the apex domain later. Leave APP_HOST
# and APP_URL unset unless you deliberately split the app onto app.<domain> (AGENTS.md → "Domain topology").
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://appealdeck.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_HOST=appealdeck.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_HOST=app.appealdeck.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://app.appealdeck.com

# --- Cloud LLM (Gemini, backend only; key NEVER shipped to client bundle) ---
# Get your key at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey. PRODUCTION IS ON THE PAID TIER (assumed on
# the founder's word, 26 Oct 2026, NOT verified by any code): the privacy policy promises it, and
# Google's paid tier does not use prompts or documents to improve its products
# (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §6b, decision D9). Confirm the key's Google Cloud project in AI Studio and
# Cloud Billing before setting the flag below. Keep development keys in
# a separate free-tier project with test documents only, so a seller's document can never reach one.
# Production still refuses every Gemini call until GEMINI_PAID_TIER_CONFIRMED=true, because no key
# can prove its tier. The breaker in src/lib/breaker.ts caps daily request volume — see
# breakerOptions in src/lib/llm/gemini.ts.
# Verified working on a new key 4 Sep 2026 (returned 200 OK to a real generateContent call).
# Verified NOT working: gemini-2.5-flash and gemini-2.5-flash-lite both 404 on new keys ("no longer
# available to new users"). gemini-flash-latest 503s under load. The models below are the measured
# choices per task, not a tier: gemini-3.5-flash (the default), gemini-3.5-flash-lite (lighter) and
# gemini-flash-lite-latest (latest alias of the lite).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
# Asked once when the main model is busy, stalls or is over its quota. Blank = gemini-3-flash-preview;
# "none" switches it off.
GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODEL=
# Optional per-task model overrides (read in src/lib/llm/gemini.ts); blank = GEMINI_MODEL.
GEMINI_MODEL_READ_DOCUMENT=
GEMINI_MODEL_IMPROVE_WORDING=
GEMINI_MODEL_DRAFT_POA=
# Reasoning tokens for the drafting call (Plan of Action, document-request explanation, questionnaire
# answers). Blank or 0 = off, the measured-stable setting (a schema-mode call with thinking on stalled
# on 25 Sep and 9 Oct 2026). Try 1024 on the paid tier and compare with the evaluation harness.
GEMINI_DRAFT_THINKING=
# Production only: set to true after confirming the key's Google Cloud project is on the paid tier
# (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §6b). Until then every Gemini call is refused in production. Ignored in dev.
GEMINI_PAID_TIER_CONFIRMED=

# Second AI provider for text tasks only; never receives PDFs or images. It answers when Gemini is
# over quota, down, or rejects its key. A second Groq model (own rate limit) is tried before giving up.
# In production it also needs GROQ_PRODUCTION_CONFIRMED=true, set only after the privacy policy names
# Groq as a processor (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §6c).
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b
GROQ_FALLBACK_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
GROQ_PRODUCTION_CONFIRMED=

# --- Supabase (server-side admin client) ---
# Paid plan assumed (26 Oct 2026): no free-project pause and provider backups on. Our own encrypted
# dump workflow still runs nightly (DEPLOYMENT.md §6a): it covers the paid rows, Supabase's backup
# covers auth.users. Migrations 0016-0026 are manual pastes (GO-LIVE-REGISTER step 0).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Rate limiting (Upstash Redis; the free tier's 10k req/day and 1 region are enough for launch) ---
# Missing configuration bypasses limits only in development; production denies limited requests.
# One database is enough. The Vercel Storage integration may inject the KV_* names instead.
# REQUIRED in Vercel production for the cloud breaker to actually cap spend.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
# The Vercel Storage integration names the same two values KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN;
# src/lib/redisEnv.ts reads either pair, so set one pair, not both.
KV_REST_API_URL=
KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# --- Merchant of record (primary: Paddle) ---
# Paddle approval is assumed done (26 Oct 2026); approval creates no product, price, client token or
# webhook. Run scripts/setup-paddle-live.mjs, then set the default payment link (GO-LIVE-REGISTER
# step 2). Production values go in Vercel production; sandbox values stay in .env.local for local
# testing. Guardian is deferred under D7 and nothing reads its price, so there is none.
PADDLE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_APPEAL_PASS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_ENV=production

# Every other product is sold only when its price id is set (blank = not sold; its card shows
# "Opens soon" or disappears). Apply the matching migration before setting one. Prices must equal
# src/content/purchases.ts; tests recompute the derived ones. Steps: docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §5c–§5f.
# One Response $99 · Pass after One Response $150 · Account Pass $329 · renewal $99
# AI review $49 · Pass after a review $200 · 10 credits $390 · 30 credits $870 ·
# Pro plan $349/month (a subscription)
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_SINGLE_RESPONSE=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_PASS_AFTER_SINGLE=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_ACCOUNT_PASS=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_ACCOUNT_RENEWAL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_DOCUMENT_REVIEW=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_PASS_AFTER_REVIEW=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_PACK_10=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_PACK_30=
NEXT_PUBLIC_PADDLE_PRICE_PRO_PLAN=
# Founding offer (optional): USD 80 off the Account Pass, usage limit must equal SPOTS (default 25).
NEXT_PUBLIC_FOUNDING_CODE=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FOUNDING_SPOTS=
# The $25 outcome rebate is a partial refund made by hand; this only shows its wording.
NEXT_PUBLIC_REBATE_ENABLED=false

# Optional referral ledger. Apply migrations through 0026 before enabling (0023 first; 0024 adds
# the linked-refund rules). The server key needs discount.read; it also powers the verified
# founding-offer count.
PADDLE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_REFERRALS_ENABLED=false
# Products with no Paddle price yet are shown with their price and a disabled "Opens soon" button,
# so the whole structure is visible before each payment connection exists (founder's decision, kept
# 26 Oct 2026). Nothing unsold can be bought: every purchase path needs its Paddle price.
# Set to `off` to hide those cards until a price is configured.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PLANS_PREVIEW=off

# --- Analytics (D10's funnel measurement; client-side, cookieless) ---
# Added 11 Sep 2026. Sign up at https://plausible.io (paid, no free tier) or self-host the open-
# source Community Edition (free — see src/content/legal.ts's privacy disclosure, which names
# "Plausible or Umami" either way). Set this to your site's domain exactly as Plausible expects it
# (e.g. "appealdeck.com"). Without it, no analytics script loads at all — src/components/
# AnalyticsScript.tsx renders nothing, and src/lib/analytics.ts's trackFunnelEvent no-ops silently.
NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN=

# --- Transactional email (D8's required purchase-confirmation email; server-side only) ---
# Added 11 Sep 2026 — the checkout has always promised "you will receive a receipt and a copy
# of this consent by email" (src/content/legal.ts) but nothing sent it until src/lib/email.ts.
# Sign up at https://resend.com, verify appealdeck.com as the sending domain (DNS), and set both vars
# below. Without RESEND_API_KEY, purchase provisioning still succeeds and the durable
# outbox retains unsent confirmations for retry. Configure CRON_SECRET on the deployed project.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# Where the daily ops digest goes when a payment is parked or an email keeps failing (needs
# RESEND_API_KEY too). Without it the counts are written to the Vercel logs as an error line.
OPS_ALERT_EMAIL=
EMAIL_FROM=AppealDeck <billing@appealdeck.com>
# Replies go here. Defaults to billing@appealdeck.com when unset; set it if replies should reach a
# different person. The purchase email's 14-day refund offer relies on a reply arriving.
EMAIL_REPLY_TO=billing@appealdeck.com
# Protects the scheduled durable purchase-confirmation worker.
CRON_SECRET=

# ============================================================================
# LOCAL DEV ONLY (never set in deployment env)
# ============================================================================
# Created by `node scripts/seed-dev-user.mjs` on the dev Supabase project.
# Email defaults to dev@appealdeck.com; password is generated randomly and
# printed to stdout. Founder should store the password in a local password
# manager, not commit it.
DEV_LOGIN_EMAIL=
DEV_LOGIN_PASSWORD=
# Removes app usage caps only for the signed-in DEV_LOGIN_EMAIL in non-production.
# Provider quotas, Pass checks and input validation still apply.
DEV_UNLIMITED_USAGE=

# ============================================================================
# NOT USED BY THE APP — kept here for reference and removed from Vercel
# ============================================================================
# The following variables appear in older planning docs but are NOT read by
# the current codebase. Do not set them in Vercel — adds noise to the env
# dashboard and slows audits.
#
# POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN        — Polar is the warm fallback rail; account not
# POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET      — created until Paddle flips a material rate
# POLAR_PRICE_APPEAL_PASS   — limit. See AGENTS.md §"Payment Rails (D2)".
# PAYMENTS_PROVIDER         — Single-rail MVP. Always Paddle. Switch on
#                             failure to migrate, not via env var.
# SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF      — Used only by local `supabase` CLI; not at
#                             runtime.
# SUPABASE_DB_DUMP_ENCRYPTION_KEY — Backup encryption is handled by Supabase
#                             Pro / manual pg_dump; no code reads this.
# ANALYTICS_SCRIPT_SRC      — not read. Analytics is wired through
# ANALYTICS_HOST            — NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN above.
#
# --- MCP-only (local CLI tooling, not consumed by the app) ---
# GITHUB_TOKEN              — kilo MCP server (local)
# OPENAI_API_KEY            — kilo / browser-use MCP (local)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY         — kilo / browser-use MCP (local)
# CAL_API_KEY               — Cal.com MCP (local)
# VERCEL_API_KEY            — Vercel MCP (local)
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN     — Supabase MCP (local)
# DATABASE_URL              — Postgres MCP (local)
# SENTRY_ACCESS_TOKEN       — Sentry MCP (local)
# POSTHOG_API_KEY           — PostHog MCP (local)
# MEM0_API_KEY              — Mem0 MCP (local)
# EMAIL_IMAP_HOST/USER/PASS — Email MCP (local)
# EMAIL_SMTP_HOST/USER/PASS — Email MCP (local)
# EMBEDDED_AGENT_PROVIDER   — kilo internal (not used by app code)
# Countries where checkout is refused (comma-separated ISO codes). Unset: the EU, the rest of the EEA and
# the UK. Set to `none` on the day those markets open. See src/lib/region.ts.
BLOCKED_PURCHASE_COUNTRIES=
